    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_media_framing_bias_distancing",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-media-framing-bias-01",
        "slug": "c1-media-framing-bias-distancing",
        "title": "Distancing from claims",
        "rule_summary": "Use apparently, reportedly, according to, it would seem, and claims that to avoid presenting uncertain information as your own fact.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای اینکه اطلاعات نامطمئن را واقعیت قطعی خودمان نشان ندهیم از apparently، reportedly، according to، it would seem و claims that استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "According to the review, the benefits were unevenly distributed.",
            "fa": "طبق بررسی، مزایا به‌طور نابرابر توزیع شده بود."
          },
          {
            "en": "It would seem that the original estimate was too optimistic.",
            "fa": "به نظر می‌رسد برآورد اولیه بیش از حد خوش‌بینانه بوده است."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_media_framing_bias_advanced_reporting",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-media-framing-bias-02",
        "slug": "c1-media-framing-bias-advanced-reporting",
        "title": "Advanced reporting verbs",
        "rule_summary": "Choose reporting verbs such as acknowledge, maintain, concede, dispute, imply, and caution to represent a source's stance accurately.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای بازتاب دقیق موضع منبع از فعل‌هایی مثل acknowledge، maintain، concede، dispute، imply و caution استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The author acknowledges the limitation but maintains that the trend is meaningful.",
            "fa": "نویسنده محدودیت را می‌پذیرد اما همچنان معتقد است روند معنادار است."
          },
          {
            "en": "The report cautions against treating correlation as proof of cause.",
            "fa": "گزارش هشدار می‌دهد همبستگی را به‌عنوان اثبات علت در نظر نگیریم."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_media_framing_bias_cleft_sentences",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-media-framing-bias-03",
        "slug": "c1-media-framing-bias-cleft-sentences",
        "title": "Cleft sentences for focus",
        "rule_summary": "Use what-clauses and it-clefts to place deliberate emphasis on the most important part of a message.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با what-clause و it-cleft بخش مهم پیام را برجسته می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "What concerns me most is the lack of independent oversight.",
            "fa": "چیزی که بیشتر نگرانم می‌کند نبود نظارت مستقل است."
          },
          {
            "en": "It was the timing, rather than the decision itself, that caused the problem.",
            "fa": "زمان‌بندی بود، نه خود تصمیم، که مشکل را ایجاد کرد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
